{
  "ballPalette": "ash",
  "virgil": {"height":41,"lines":[["Virgil","Do you not ask who these spirits are? They did not sin, but they did not receive baptism. Those who lived before Christianity did not worship God as you do. I am one of them."],["Virgil","We live in desire without hope."],["Ball","Has anyone ever left this place and gone on to be blessed, through their own merit or another's?"],["Virgil","I was new here when a mighty one came crowned with victory. He led away Adam, Abel, Noah, Moses, Abraham, David, and many others, and made them blessed."],["Virgil","Two levers open the castle gate. One is among the sighs, and the other lies beyond the poets' fire."]],"beats":{"egg":[["Ball","There was something shining in the dust."],["Virgil","A small light can show a way through the dark. Follow where the next one leads."]],"mist":[["Ball","I pulled the lever among the sighs."],["Virgil","That chain runs to the castle. There is another beyond the poets' fire."]],"ember":[["Ball","I moved the lever beyond the fire."],["Virgil","The chain leads back toward the castle. The two together will lift the gate."]],"poets-fire":[["Ball","They made room for me among them."],["Virgil","Remember the welcome. We have farther to go."]],"relief":[["Ball","The sixth alcove is lit."],["Virgil","Look deeper into the chamber. Something has opened in its light."]],"rose":[["Ball","The rose is warm."],["Virgil","Carry it with you. You may remember this warmth when the air turns cold."]],"trial-start":[["Virgil","The old stones are giving way. Watch the dust rise before you cross."]],"trial-clear":[["Ball","The stones held long enough."],["Virgil","Beyond the meadow the quiet ends. We must descend."]]}},
