    {"name":"Homer","x":1215,"y":761,"height":51,"robe":"#b38b72","prop":"sword","lines":[["Ball","You who honor every art and science, who are these people who are held in such honor apart from the rest?"],["Virgil","Their good names still sound among the living. That earns them favor in Heaven."],["A voice","Honor the great poet. His shade returns."],["Virgil","The one with the sword is Homer. Then come Horace the satirist, Ovid, and Lucan."],["Narrator","They greet Virgil and welcome the ball as the sixth of their company. The words they exchange stay between them."]],"id":"poets-fire","label":"Listen to the poets"},
